Chapter: Allocator

 Phase-allocator primitives. Step 1 of the phase-discipline migration —
 thin wrappers over the existing bump allocator with no callers in this
 chapter. See docs/Active/Compiler/PHASE-ARCHITECTURE.md.

 pitch / strike enclose a bivy (phase-local scratch).
 build / seal enclose a deck (phase-durable contribution).

 No callers yet — every primitive here is dead until a phase routes
 through it. The runtime support that gives strike teeth on bare metal
 (un-no-oping __heap-restore, the deck-pos cell, emit-record's
 deck-bound branch) lives in a companion changelist.

Section: Bivy

 pitch saves the bump pointer and reserves `size` bytes upfront. The
 size argument is a hint, not a hard cap: the phase can allocate more
 above the col while it runs (the bivy grows up from `p`), and strike
 rolls everything past `p` back. Today, strike on bare metal is a
 no-op (matching __heap-restore as it is currently emitted), so the
 `size` reservation in pitch effectively burns those bytes from the
 heap permanently — that is acceptable because nothing calls pitch
 yet. Once strike acquires real semantics in the runtime CL, pitch
 starts reclaiming on every call.

  pitch : Integer -> Integer
  pitch (size) =
   let p = __heap-save
   in let advanced = __heap-advance size
   in p

  strike : Integer -> Nothing
  strike (start) =
   __heap-restore start

Section: Deck

 build reserves a deck region of `size` bytes by advancing the bump
 pointer, and points the deck-pos cell at the deck start so that
 deck-record allocations land in the deck rather than the bivy. The
 source-level distinction (build = deck = surveyed and durable,
 pitch = bivy = scratch) is the contract readers see; today the only
 runtime distinction is the __deck-set call. seal is a placeholder
 that emits a no-op via __heap-advance 0; once the escape-invariant
 enforcement lands seal will validate that no deck slot points into
 the bivy and atomically commit the deck.

  build : Integer -> Integer
  build (size) =
   let p = __heap-save
   in let deck-init = __deck-set p
   in let advanced = __heap-advance size
   in p

  seal : Integer -> Nothing
  seal (start) =
   __heap-advance 0

Section: Deck-bound record allocation

 Marker for record literals that must be allocated from the deck
 pointer instead of the bivy bump pointer. Self-host's emit-apply
 special-cases the name and routes the wrapped expression through
 deck-bound codegen. As a plain user function this is just identity,
 which is what every backend that does not implement the special-case
 will emit and what runs on .NET where the bump-pointer distinction
 does not exist.

  deck-record : a -> a
  deck-record (x) =
   x

